    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nSince Cython 3.1.0, importing any compiled module in a Python 3.8 debug build (`--with-pydebug`) fails a CPython assertion while the `cython_function_or_method` type is created:\n```\nObjects/typeobject.c:5259: PyType_Ready: Assertion \"type->tp_vectorcall_offset > 0\" failed\n```\n\n(The segfault comes from CPython printing the half-initialised type after the failed assertion.)\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```bash\npython3.8d -m venv venv\nvenv/bin/python -m pip install \"cython==3.2.9\"\nvenv/bin/python -m cython --version\n```\n`python3.8d` is a debug build (can be built as `./configure --with-pydebug && make install` or installed as `python3.8-dbg` on Debian/Ubuntu)\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCompiled modules import under a Python 3.8 debug build, as they do with Cython 3.0.x or Python 3.9+.\n\n### OS\n\nLinux (RHEL 9, x86_64)\n\n### Python version\n\n3.8.20 (`--with-pydebug`)\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.2.9\n\n### Additional context\n\nThe assertion is in [CPython 3.8](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.8.20/Objects/typeobject.c#L5258-L5261).\n`master` no longer supports Python 3.8, so this affects the 3.1.x and 3.2.x series.",
