            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It'll be to do with the need to fixup heap types because vectorcalloffset isn't applied correctly on Python 3.8.\n\nhttps://github.com/cython/cython/blob/a827026cdd80134b12721adb8d43ce0504c23ab0/Cython/Utility/ExtensionTypes.c#L10\n\nTo be honest, at this point I don't think it's worth fixing unless it's *very very very* easy (like <5 extremely obvious lines of code level of easy...). Py3.8 is old enough and debug builds are rare enough. And the issue is mostly because we're working around a defect in Python 3.8",
